fix-sm2-p256-kdf-hash: no unimplemented SM3 in the KDF of TPM2_ECC_Parameters(SM2 P-256)

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2, "TPMI_ALG_HASH"):

  "TPMI_ALG_HASH is an interface type of all the hash algorithms
  implemented on a specific TPM. ... if the algorithm is not implemented in
  a specific TPM, that algorithm is not included in the interface type."

and Part 2, "TPMS_ALGORITHM_DETAIL_ECC", kdf: "the default KDF and hash
algorithm recommended for use in secret sharing operations (may be
TPM_ALG_NULL)".

The recommended KDF of SM2 P-256 in the curve table is KDF1_SP800_56A with
SM3_256, which TPM2_ECC_Parameters returns even when the TPM does not
implement SM3 (ALG_SM3_256 = NO in this profile): the response then carries
a TPMI_ALG_HASH value outside the interface type, which the TPM itself
rejects on input. Without SM3 the curve has no implementable recommended
KDF, so TPM_ALG_NULL is reported (as tpm-rs does).

diff --git a/src/CryptEccData.c b/src/CryptEccData.c
index 15264b2..ca633c2 100644
--- a/src/CryptEccData.c
+++ b/src/CryptEccData.c
@@ -143,7 +143,14 @@ const TPM_ECC_CURVE_METADATA eccCurves[] = {
 #  if ECC_SM2_P256
     comma{TPM_ECC_SM2_P256,
 	    256,
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // a TPMI_ALG_HASH is an implemented hash (TPM 2.0 Part 2, "TPMI_ALG_HASH"), so
+    // without SM3 the recommended KDF of SM2 P-256 is TPM_ALG_NULL.
+#    if ALG_SM3_256
 		{TPM_ALG_KDF1_SP800_56A, {{TPM_ALG_SM3_256}}},
+#    else
+		{TPM_ALG_NULL, {{TPM_ALG_NULL}}},
+#    endif
 		    {TPM_ALG_NULL, {{TPM_ALG_NULL}}},
 	    OID_ECC_SM2_P256 CURVE_NAME("SM2_P256")}
 #    undef comma
